raphael fb: one short IOLog pacing line per stats window

kern.sweet_fb carries every counter, but the line is longer than one UDP datagram on the
USB log link, so the tail (gpu_holds, swap_wait_us, latch_us, copy_us, zc_us) never arrives
in the captured console log. Print the pacing numbers on their own short line once per
window instead: frames held by the scan-out gate for the GPU fence (and how many hit the
50 ms cap), the average SwapWait and latch wait, and the per-frame copy/zero-copy time.
A high gpu_holds count is the compositor waiting for its own GPU work, which looks like a
busy GPU with a low frame rate from the outside.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -1186,6 +1225,16 @@
 	    fScanGpu && !fScanGpuOff ? (fScanGpuRest ? 2 : 1) : 0, c.scanGpuCopies, c.scanGpuFallbacks,
 	    c.scanGpuSubmitFails, c.scanGpuLate, sweet_abs_us(c.scanGpuWaitMaxAbs));
 	#undef PER_S
+	/*
+	 * Pacing line (patch 0264): one short IOLog line per stats window with the numbers that
+	 * decide how a frame reaches the panel. kern.sweet_fb has all of them, but the full line
+	 * does not fit a single UDP datagram on the USB log link and gets split. gpu_holds/hold_to
+	 * count frames the scan-out gate held for the GPU fence (50 ms cap): a high count is the
+	 * compositor waiting for its own GPU work, which is what a low frames-per-second with a
+	 * busy GPU looks like from the outside.
+	 */
+	IOLog("SWEET FB: pace win=%llums swaps=%llu copy=%llu zc=%llu gpu_holds=%llu hold_to=%llu swap_wait_us=%llu latch_us=%llu copy_us=%llu zc_us=%llu\n",
+	    winUS / 1000, dSwaps, dCopy, dZc, c.gpuHolds, c.gpuHoldTimeouts, swAvg, lwAvg, copyAvg, zcAvg);
 	sweet_fb_stats_publish(line);
 	if (fStLogSecs != 0 && (fStLogT == 0 || sweet_abs_us(now - fStLogT) >= (uint64_t)fStLogSecs * 1000000)) {
 		fStLogT = now;
